{"step_index":7396,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-25T15:59:40Z","thinking":"The `nvme0n1` device is the Azure Managed OS Disk, appearing as an MSFT NVMe Accelerator.  The `nvme1n1` device is identified as a \"Microsoft NVMe Direct Disk,\" which is likely the host-attached local NVMe temporary storage.\n\n\nThe ephemeral disk's `nofail` mount in `/home` is crucial; it highlights that Azure Restore Points won't capture the contents because it's not a managed disk. This means `/home` requires independent backups to a vault or data disk. The findings emphasize the importance of Phases 6 and 4 for comprehensive coverage.\n\nNow, investigating Phase 1, the goal is to create a GCP Machine Image directly via the Service Account using Python and the Compute Engine REST API. The API endpoint for machine image creation is identified, and the plan is to test this approach.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python3 -c \"\nimport json, time, urllib.request, urllib.parse, urllib.error, jwt\n\nwith open('/home/azureuser/.config/rclone/service_account.json') as f:\n    sa = json.load(f)\n\nnow = int(time.time())\npayload = {\n    'iss': sa['client_email'],\n    'sub': sa['client_email'],\n    'aud': sa['token_uri'],\n    'iat': now,\n    'exp': now + 3600,\n    'scope': 'https://www.googleapis.com/auth/cloud-platform'\n}\nsigned_jwt = jwt.encode(payload, sa['private_key'], algorithm='RS256')\ndata = urllib.parse.urlencode({\n    'grant_type': 'urn:ietf:params:oauth:grant-type:jwt-bearer',\n    'assertion': signed_jwt\n}).encode()\nreq = urllib.request.Request(sa['token_uri'], data=data)\ntoken = json.loads(urllib.request.urlopen(req).read())['access_token']\n\n# Check if image already exists\nurl_check = 'https://compute.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/irak-mahmud-project/global/machineImages/gcp-vm-full-backup-20260925'\nreq_check = urllib.request.Request(url_check, headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}'})\ntry:\n    resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req_check)\n    print('Machine Image ALREADY EXISTS:', resp.read().decode()[:300])\nexcept urllib.error.HTTPError as e:\n    print('Check Machine Image HTTP:', e.code)\n    if e.code == 404:\n        print('Machine image does not exist yet. Attempting creation...')\n        url_create = 'https://compute.googleapis.com/compute/v1/projects/irak-mahmud-project/global/machineImages'\n        body = {\n            'name': 'gcp-vm-full-backup-20260925',\n            'sourceInstance': 'projects/irak-mahmud-project/zones/us-central1-a/instances/instance-20260925-131309'\n        }\n        req_create = urllib.request.Request(\n            url_create,\n            data=json.dumps(body).encode(),\n            headers={'Authorization': f'Bearer {token}', 'Content-Type': 'application/json'},\n            method='POST'\n        )\n        try:\n            r = urllib.request.urlopen(req_create)\n            print('Creation triggered successfully:', r.read().decode())\n        except urllib.error.HTTPError as err:\n            print('Creation failed HTTP:', err.code, err.read().decode())\n    else:\n        print('Error checking:', e.read().decode())\n\"","Cwd":"/home/azureuser","RequestedTerminalID":"","RunPersistent":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":10000,"toolAction":"Testing GCP Machine Image creation","toolSummary":"Check and create GCP Machine Image"}}]}
